# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Vampyre Slayer" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Morgan	Could it be? A bold adventurer! Please, you must help us!
1	line	Player	What is it? What's the problem?
1	line	Morgan	It's the evil vampyre, Count Draynor! For too long he's terrorised us from his manor to the north. Someone finally needs to put a stop to him once and for all!
1	cond	If the player has a combat level less than 20:
2	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 20.
1	select	Start the Vampyre Slayer quest?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Sounds like a job for me. Where should I start?
2	line	Morgan	Oh, thank goodness! I've been hoping this day would come for a long time, so I've made sure to do my research. I've heard of a retired vampyre hunter called Dr Harlow who lives in Varrock.
2	line	Morgan	If you speak to him, I'm sure he'll be able to help. I hear he's a bit of an old soak these days, so he spends most of his time in the Blue Moon Inn.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	What else can you tell me about this vampyre?
3	line	Player	What else can you tell me about this vampyre?
3	line	Morgan	All sorts of things! I've studied the legends extensively!
3	line	Player	Wait... legends? What do you mean legends?
3	line	Morgan	The legends of Count Draynor! It's said that long ago, he travelled here from dark lands in the east. He built Draynor Manor, and from there he began his campaign of darkness against our peaceful lands!
3	line	Player	Long ago? If this has been going on for so long, why has no one tried to stop him?
3	line	Morgan	Many have tried. All have failed. Vampyres are not killed easily. Only those with the right skills and equipment have any hope of slaying one.
3	line	Player	Like this Dr Harlow? Home come he's never tried to kill this Count Draynor?
3	line	Morgan	I'm... not sure. Perhaps he was always too busy killing other vampyres?
3	line	Player	Hmm... Something seems amiss here. Are you sure you're telling me everything?
3	line	Morgan	Well... it is true that some claim Count Draynor hasn't left his manor for generations now.
3	line	Player	So he's not actually attacked the village?
3	line	Morgan	Er... no. At least, not for a long time! He used to though!
3	line	Player	When?
3	line	Morgan	Well... not since I've moved here at least.
3	line	Player	So if there's no actual danger, why are you so keen for someone to kill this vampyre?
3	line	Morgan	Because what if he does start attacking again? Are we just meant to live our lives constantly fearing the future?
3	line	Player	It doesn't really sound like anyone is living in fear apart from you.
3	line	Morgan	More fool them! Count Draynor has cast a shadow over Draynor Village for generations. They even named the place after him for Saradomin's sake!
3	line	Morgan	Even if the people here don't realise it, we will never be at peace until we know he's dead!
3	line	Player	If you're sure... I guess I'll go and see this Dr Harlow.
3	line	Morgan	Thank you, brave adventurer.
3	action	end
2	option	Alright, I'll see about paying him a visit.
3	line	Player	Alright, I'll see about paying him a visit.
3	line	Morgan	Thank you, brave adventurer.
3	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	An evil vampyre? I don't think this is the job for me. It sounds far too scary!
2	line	Morgan	I understand... Hopefully someone else will come along to finally save us from this evil.
2	action	end
